cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, cite it as below."
title: "NeuroBranch: leakage-safe C. elegans dynamics and bounded virtual-perturbation evaluation"
abstract: >-
  NeuroBranch is a research platform for C. elegans whole-brain population
  dynamics, latent branching and model-dependent virtual perturbation. Version
  1.1.0 adds coverage-aware variance components, a two-way uncertainty audit,
  benchmark-card provenance and a machine-readable claims ledger. The Phase 11
  analysis shows that the pooled reliability ceiling is sensitive to sparse
  responder coverage (0.560 at 80% coverage, not the Phase 10 value of 0.833).
  Intervention outputs are model-dependent and are not causally validated.
authors:
  - name: "NeuroBranch contributors"
version: "1.1.0"
date-released: "2026-10-29"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - computational neuroscience
  - C. elegans
  - calcium imaging
  - optogenetics
  - reliability
  - benchmark
type: software
